go 1.25.0

// The workspace composes the SDK and the product modules from source during
// local development, so a change to the SDK is testable before it is tagged.
//
// It declares no replacements. It used to replace an SDK version that had never
// been published, because the Go tool cannot build a module graph that requires
// a version with no revision. sdk/v0.1.0 exists now, so a module requires a
// version the module proxy can serve and the replacement is gone. Committed
// replace directives remain prohibited in every go.mod; see
// docs/plans/first-cli-vertical-slice.md section 4 and
// docs/adr/0009-sdk-versioning-and-publication.md.
use (
	.
	./modules/reference
	./sdk
)
